From 107beb3272b778a41b9f1d768590635eb3ef4691 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 10:47:33 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] yblod-engine-vk: run without push descriptors and without
 VAAPI (Raspberry Pi 5)

- VK_KHR_push_descriptor is optional: without it (v3dv) each dispatch binds a
  descriptor set from pools owned by its command buffer, reset when the
  command buffer is. DVVK_NO_PUSH_DESCRIPTOR=1 forces this path.
- dvvk_set_surface_dmabuf: decoders without VAAPI register decoded pictures
  (DRM PRIME layout) by id; engines created with va_display NULL use them.
- DRM_FORMAT_P030 + BROADCOM_SAND128 (the Pi 5 HEVC decoder's 10-bit
  output, which v3dv cannot import as an image): imported as buffers and
  unpacked each frame by sand30_unpack.comp into P010-identical planes.
